Config.fromEnv : '{IO} Config   ~gmcoc20cda
  ! reads UNIDORK_* env vars with HARDCODED fallbacks baked into the source (db host localhost, port 5434, user postgres, name dork; specific NAS paths under /home/bismuth). nix/config.nix is expected to set these env vars; the literals here are last-resort defaults, not the production config.
  ! performs IO (getEnv) and never fails: every missing var resolves to its fallback.
  ! the movie/tv format strings are also fallback literals here; production format strings come from UNIDORK_FORMAT_MOVIE / UNIDORK_FORMAT_TV.

Config.getEnvOr : Text -> Text ->{IO} Text   ~cg0o7c2dpo
  ! empty OR whitespace-only env values are treated as UNSET and resolve to the fallback (Text.trim then size==0 check), not returned as empty strings.
